    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Top queries by average latency",
      "description": "topk(10, pg_stat_statements_seconds_total / pg_stat_statements_calls_total), joined against pg_stat_statements_query_id (queryid → query text) via a joinByField transformation — the classic \"which single execution is slow\" ranking. Both sides of the division share the exact same {user, datname, queryid} label set, so no aggregation/label-mismatch is needed to make the division safe (unlike several earlier panels in this dashboard). Needs the postgres-exporter service's --collector.stat_statements flag AND the pg_stat_statements extension created in appdata (see docker-compose.yml's postgres/postgres-exporter services) — empty otherwise. The joined table may show a couple of extra raw columns (a second Time/Value pair from the lookup side); hide or reorder them from the panel's own field-organize UI if you want it tidier.",
